{"title":"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 9","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Rigorous_and_easy)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Rigorous and easy)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5_(No_Fancy_Tricks)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5 (No Fancy Tricks)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/0/6d0382f3585219947b495ac2262a81b7b0c40db2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/1/8d1d002db36c51a77f8fbc6314e96756fc793e28.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"13\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be positive real numbers that satisfy\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/4/0040698f1dfdbbb5d2fe34839edc567e8818e9ae.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\log_{x}(2y) = 2\\log_{2x}(4z) = \\log_{2x^4}(8yz) \\ne 0.\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />\nThe value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/5/a3546308df0c25649ca5ab31cabdcc512e6f4c7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^5z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"38\" height=\"20\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/e/f3e3b0ec22b39c06086829bcce939a3f319efa3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2^{p/q}},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043f651be7ed631a58104b324d1aa6c6c843beba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since there are only two dependent equations given and three unknowns, the three expressions given can equate to any common value (that isn't 0, of course), so to simplify the problem let us assume without loss of generality that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e7b810a6d2b978439468b4ddc05ea235f7a990.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\log_{x}(2y) = 2\\log_{2x}(4z) = \\log_{2x^4}(8yz) = 2.\\]\" width=\"331\" height=\"18\" />\nThen\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/c/1ecb2dcb0d1cc3d187f8e5c9b78c3c41f7568fb4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} 2\\log_{x}(2y) = 2 &amp;\\implies x=2y\\\\ 2\\log_{2x}(4z) = 2 &amp;\\implies 2x=4z\\\\ \\log_{2x^4}(8yz) = 2 &amp;\\implies 4x^8 = 8yz \\end{align*}\" width=\"247\" height=\"70\" />\nSolving these equations, we quickly see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/a/13ac497e15e43cb1714e84e3dd3c584b841793e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4x^8 = (2y)(4z) = x(2x) \\rightarrow x=2^{-1/6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"286\" height=\"20\" /> and then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/2/7323c4dd3271788819eb7f593ba6d0eb22fb16bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=z=2^{-1/6 - 1} = 2^{-7/6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"192\" height=\"19\" />\nFinally, our desired value is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/9/2c9f2505662a7c100c30c916d7758e92d8c9c16b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^{-1/6} \\cdot (2^{-7/6})^5 \\cdot 2^{-7/6} = 2^{-43/6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" /> and thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/4/9b49932708c42bb0e30f294a0810f92b597c650b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q = 43 + 6 = \\boxed{049.}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/8/9987caee2d72f16ef8c84c800d2952a6c6689397.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2y\\cdot 4z=8yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15daedc53aa1877815ea9c14c838d44c129fa63d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log_2(2y)=\\log_2\\left(4y^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"174\" height=\"22\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/3/f/13f9b8d1756b03a2e5ad1f4e9698d19fd97f9282.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log_2(4z)=\\log_2\\left(16z^2\\right)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"182\" height=\"22\" />.\n</p><p>From this, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/1/d417474f54724f4956a18e021adc871ca0fcbc83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8yz$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"16\" /> is the geometric mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/8/e285b8704afb67b4c3cfe19275170bbb0c5b9f55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4y^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/f/54fc75429dcffc924b2bcd041cd9941544864c6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"33\" height=\"15\" />. So, for constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/1/081f8ac22a72e498633b7bdffb074e4abb0a5df6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\ne 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"47\" height=\"17\" />:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/f/23f39de85e1f5f39b0ad00fc3dec565c1fa27e81.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log 4y^2}{\\log x}=\\frac{\\log 8yz}{\\log 2x^4}=\\frac{\\log 16z^2}{\\log 2x}=C\\]\" width=\"265\" height=\"42\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a445697b235081f7c750eea55ad527e3889159f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log 4y^2,\\log 8yz,\\log 16z^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" /> are in an geometric progression (ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d996b637792465c05f64f41327f46ac9ae3600a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2z}{y}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"24\" height=\"42\" />), so are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/5/c751291438735db98f1a78e5e3169e9cae1ed018.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log x,\\log 2x^4,\\log 2x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"152\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1820f16f618dad73aa0a6337c4a0e5c9892dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x^4$\" width=\"26\" height=\"15\" /> is the geometric mean of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/a/6aa1d19c23f1d7a482fca4d2460fcd349ff5f9e1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2x^4=\\sqrt{x\\cdot 2x}\\implies 4x^8=2x^2\\implies 2x^6=1\\implies x=2^{-1/6}\\]\" width=\"469\" height=\"18\" />\nWe can plug <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> in to any of the two equal fractions aforementioned. So, without loss of generality:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/c/d3c7bf3b80a83d1eb8d4616b8e065aeb08c60a7d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log 4y^2}{\\log x}=\\frac{\\log 16z^2}{\\log 2x}\\implies \\log\\left(4y^2\\right)\\log\\left(2x\\right)=\\log\\left(16z^2\\right)\\log\\left(x\\right)\\]\" width=\"480\" height=\"42\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65bdb7a5d6d9e2b9ad1a72414128c53e88e0555.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\log\\left(4y^2\\right)\\cdot \\frac{5}{6}\\log 2=\\log\\left(16z^2\\right)\\cdot \\frac{-1}{6}\\log 2\\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/f/bcfd0aba1264651023e6d4a00201d0f1b6eba82c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies 5\\log\\left(4y^2\\right)=-\\log\\left(16z^2\\right)\\implies 5\\log\\left(4y^2\\right)+\\log\\left(16z^2\\right)=0\\]\" width=\"493\" height=\"22\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/b/10b7a5e6a5bb13f1b2fe0cf82101e9ce41f31649.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\implies \\left(4y^2\\right)^5\\cdot 16z^2=1\\implies 16384y^{10}z^2=1\\implies y^{10}z^2=\\frac{1}{16384}\\implies y^5z=\\frac{1}{128}\\]\" width=\"623\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/8/c386efbe3c822c31310f28add86b737d43fd5da4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^5z=2^{-\\frac{1}{6}-7}=2^{-\\frac{43}{6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"165\" height=\"21\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac4659601fc392c051ebb5cd749d1949047b9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$43+6=\\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/0/d20258310be3455daf8318274224a9d1d28fb6a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y, z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"11\" /> are positive real numbers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> can be expressed as powers of two.  We shall thus let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/8/7c8e50e12978e1ef5b43e2800cd812d663119752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 2^X$\" width=\"54\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/d/0fdab5696ca231d1b07b991c67679ded7d33b221.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 2^Y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"18\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/4/744ff43f17b90044eb69ef1cc782f2f5a6a1bc95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 2^Z$\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />.  Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d012f9c64189fb9301dde0f1def481c33f13e44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = \\log_{2^X}(2^{Y+1})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"125\" height=\"19\" />.  From this we get the system of equations: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/f/57f1406b65f9f2e6a365b7356da731780b42cceb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\]\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/3/3734ddd564860a9cd4d15f3bc69558510ca3eabf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\log_{2^X}(2^{Y+1}) \\Rightarrow aX = Y + 1\\]\" width=\"250\" height=\"19\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/8/ac8000162ea2d1e5b6385546e78a7838d9ea1d82.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a = \\log_{2^{X + 1}}(2^{Z + 2}) \\Rightarrow aX + a = Z + 2\\]\" width=\"295\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/c/51c264c5b9711c54196d0b4be468dc9fd6fa5198.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2a = \\log_{2^{4X + 1}}(2^{Y + Z + 3}) \\Rightarrow 8aX + 2a = Y + Z + 3\\]\" width=\"385\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Plugging equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> into equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/6/0d68ffa5cf9ace5d2f0a2dd9a75bb4ed799b104d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y + a = Z + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"114\" height=\"14\" />.  Plugging equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> into equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and simplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/7/397bcacbc8afefcc11334f7723c03de41b375db1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7Y + 2a + 6 = Z + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"164\" height=\"14\" />, and substituting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/9/c795cfdda5270092ea98c2f53954d149532f5d93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y + a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/d/e2d61c67d97aa4e492b1cf87ec3341a02901be8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> and simplifying yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/8/8681ebce8335d0f5e8d88c046ec3cce93c902b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y + 1 = \\frac{-a}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"96\" height=\"33\" />.  But <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/8/0981f460afe0f3e9ea63be31d6f1941a95a43b17.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Y + 1 = aX$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"95\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/5/5d5d8403f8d1bbead2a1d2fcd50439b872409d91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$aX =  \\frac{-a}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"76\" height=\"33\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f980201f21250249f69b8828160b358a204f5c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = \\frac{-1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p><p>Knowing this, we may substitute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/464195ed60cacce55d588d08e61f51836d363fa9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"25\" height=\"37\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> in equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, yielding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/d/84d02daccd0679e042524ca584d66cec165b52e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{-a}{6} = Y + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/5/ac5044590921a7d0642bdf4ffee20c7a3b3f054f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{5a}{6} = Z + 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"94\" height=\"38\" />.  Thus, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/d/1ed1c9f040680781b4699cff1d82bcc799be3162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-5(Y + 1) = Z + 2 \\rightarrow 5Y + Z = -7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"287\" height=\"18\" />.  We are looking for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/8/5887c02c1179717d805a2a8bd9930acb41ca6bf1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^5z = 2^{X+ 5Y + Z}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"129\" height=\"18\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/9/1f980201f21250249f69b8828160b358a204f5c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X = \\frac{-1}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"66\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0d49cccd04dd66cf4f2d96322a79ea0fdfdb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5Y + Z = -7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"107\" height=\"14\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/3/6c3d4ffd43a1b77df4642253c1bec74549bd5ac2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^5z = 2^{-43/6} = \\frac{1}{2^{43/6}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"171\" height=\"37\" />.  The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac4659601fc392c051ebb5cd749d1949047b9a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$43+6=\\boxed{049}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Rigorous_and_easy.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Rigorous_and_easy)\">Solution 4 (Rigorous and easy)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Rigorous and easy)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Mediant_theorem\" title=\"Mediant theorem\">Mediant theorem</a>, we know that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/c/86c4ffcde8be8f2186531692ff124e4d432bdfec.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{\\log (4y^2)}{\\log (x)} = \\frac{\\log (16z^2)}{\\log (2x)} = \\frac{2\\log (8yz)}{\\log (2x^2)}.\\]\" width=\"276\" height=\"44\" /> \n</p><p>Substituting into the original equation yields us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/0/c60188144fd923859d259e00da7fbfc6cea83ef9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{2\\log (8yz)}{\\log (2x^2)} = \\frac{\\log (8yz)}{\\log (2x^4)} \\Rightarrow 2\\log (2x^4) = \\log (2x^2) \\Rightarrow x=2^{-1/6}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"479\" height=\"45\" />\nFor some constant <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/b/63b13a0e3d88f7edaff47e36713a33c2c6721ed3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C\\not= 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"18\" /> Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/d/d/8ddcb0c1f116338206d3399654e4681b7320d764.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\log_{x}(2y) = 2\\log_{2x}(4z) = \\log_{2x^4}(8yz) = C.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"340\" height=\"20\" /> Then, we obtain the system of equations\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/0/a80c90b56ba1ad064891a0c8902960b489659de4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[y=2^{-13C/12}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/6/096a07707b2837613cc9df8fff0277423edea2b2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z=2^{-19C/12}\\]\" width=\"95\" height=\"16\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/e/b3e1c54bc3e25e149fc2c08de2ce380510903109.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[8yz=2^{C/3}.\\]\" width=\"88\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p>Multiplying the first two equations and dividing by the third, we find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/3/8339808187e6e08c7087d33c9b4019b164404198.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/7/c87a56c92e6f34ff3a83786b9f0339eead62f96d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy^5z=2^{-1/6} \\cdot 2^{-65/12} \\cdot 2^{-19/12}=2^{-43/6} \\Rightarrow p+q=\\boxed{049}.\\]\" width=\"440\" height=\"23\" />\n</p><p>~Kscv\n</p><p>~minor edits by makethan\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_5_.28No_Fancy_Tricks.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5_(No_Fancy_Tricks)\">Solution 5 (No Fancy Tricks)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5 (No Fancy Tricks)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, we can move the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />'s inside the logarithms by squaring the stuff inside: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33a65fe8ea4751460b31917e23a0a5b5f953a2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{x}(4y^2) = \\log_{2x}(16z^2) = \\log_{2x^4}(8yz)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"297\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>Setting these 3 expressions to equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, we can get rid of the logarithms by using <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/9/a9959db9d711f6e0014c9ef89469720e56f2b549.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_{a}b = c \\implies a^c = b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"174\" height=\"19\" />. The resulting equations are:\n</p><p>\\begin{align}\nx^a &amp;= 4y^2 &amp; (1) \\\\\n2^a x^a &amp;= 16z^2 &amp; (2) \\\\\n2^a x^{4a} &amp;= 8yz &amp; (3) \\\\\n\\end{align}\n</p><p>Multiplying equations <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/1/9a1f667b6e602a64fd5826dd8097f2e4167d73c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^a x^{2a} = 64y^2z^2\\]\" width=\"116\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Squaring equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/e/fbe9e9625a6968469ca8d553790798c9b78d0e57.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2^{2a} x^{8a} = 64y^2z^2\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Equating yields\n</p><p>\\begin{align}\n2^a x^{2a} &amp;= 2^{2a} x^{8a} \\\\\n2^{-a} &amp;= x^{6a} \\\\\nx &amp;= 2^{-\\frac{1}{6}} \\\\\n\\end{align}\n</p><p><br />\nDividing equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/8/b88ea3916e8089c7edbccc3ff91e58e01a6e2682.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> by equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/f/62f62a19f0425d8e6121ca0c1cfd3ce96e43c9c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/7/e1755ffd1024356d324a4061b03158d262812471.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{3a} = 2^{-1}yz^{-1}\\]\" width=\"110\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Cubing equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/9/0d9c3b1c142cbd3f8217dabc160c57e4750df241.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/3/9c3ce83b4d56e2201eea389cb437636ca2c03175.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x^{3a} = 2^6y^6\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p>Equating yields\n</p><p>\\begin{align}\n2^{-1}yz^{-1} &amp;= 2^6y^6 \\\\\nz^{-1} &amp;= 2^7y^5\\\\\nz &amp;= 2^{-7}y^{-5}\\\\\n\\end{align}\n</p><p><br />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/5/6a58fa0b68dd33e7df35a82ca90bfa00c46b41d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$xy^5z = 2^{-\\frac{1}{6}} y^5 2^{-7}y^{-5} = 2^{-\\frac{43}{6}} = \\dfrac{1}{2^{\\frac{43}{6}}} \\implies p+q = \\boxed{49}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"421\" height=\"40\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Richard_Rusczyk\">Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Richard Rusczyk\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012aimei/348\">https://artofproblemsolving.com/videos/amc/2012aimei/348</a>\n</p><p>~ dolphin7\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I\" title=\"2012 AIME I\">2012 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2012 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2012\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">Problem 10</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2012_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2012 AIME I Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017041421\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.060 seconds\nReal time usage: 1.533 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 583/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1788/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 110/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 18899/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.139      1 -total\n 59.52%    7.821      1 Template:AIME_box\n 38.58%    5.069      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10868:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017041421 and revision id 274301. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}